\lispPackageChapter{chorus/api/context}

This package initializes CUDA, selects a device, and keeps a context.
\texttt{chorus/api} reexports it.

\lispMacroSubsection{with-cuda}

\lispSyntax

\texttt{(with-cuda (\lispVar{dev-id}) \&body \lispVar{body})}

The macro calls \texttt{init-cuda}, binds \texttt{*cuda-device*} from
\texttt{dev-id}, binds \texttt{*cuda-context*}, and runs \texttt{body}. If
\texttt{*nvcc-options*} does not already name an architecture, the macro adds
the \texttt{nvcc -arch=sm\_XY} option for that device's compute capability.
On the way out it unloads \texttt{*kernel-manager*} and destroys the context.

\lispVariableSubsection{*cuda-device*}

The device selected by \texttt{with-cuda}.

\lispVariableSubsection{*cuda-context*}

The context created by \texttt{with-cuda}.

\lispVariableSubsection{*cuda-stream*}

The stream passed to kernel launches. Its initial value is a null pointer.

\lispFunctionSubsection{init-cuda}

Calls \texttt{cu-init} with flags $0$.

\lispFunctionSubsection{get-cuda-device}

Returns the device for an ordinal.

\lispFunctionSubsection{device-compute-capability}

Returns the compute capability of a device.

\lispFunctionSubsection{create-cuda-context}

Creates a context on a device.

\lispFunctionSubsection{destroy-cuda-context}

Destroys a context.

\lispFunctionSubsection{synchronize-context}

Waits until the work in the context has finished.
